---
title: Sequence diagram - forgot and reset password
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant W as Web portal<br/>ForgotPassword.jsx, ResetPassword.jsx
    participant RL as Rate limiter<br/>auth-strict, 5 per min per IP
    participant AC as AuthController
    participant AS as AuthService
    participant ES as SmtpEmailService
    participant SMTP as SMTP server<br/>(Smtp:* settings)
    participant RT as InMemoryRefreshTokenStore
    participant DB as PostgreSQL<br/>User table

    U->>W: email on /#/forgot-password
    W->>RL: POST /api/auth/forgot-password {email}
    alt rate limit exceeded
        RL-->>W: 429
    else within limit
        RL->>AC: ForgotPassword(request)
        alt email missing or invalid
            AC-->>W: 400 "A valid email address is required."
        else valid
            AC->>AS: GetUserByEmailAsync(email)
            AS->>DB: SELECT user
            opt user exists
                AC->>AC: sign reset JWT (email claim, purpose = password_reset, 30 min, Jwt:Key)
                AC->>ES: SendPasswordResetEmailAsync(email, App:BaseUrl/reset-password?token=...)
                alt Smtp:Host, Username or Password missing
                    ES->>ES: log "email simulated", send nothing
                else SMTP configured
                    ES->>SMTP: SMTP with SSL, port 587 by default
                end
            end
            AC-->>W: 200 same message whether or not the account exists
        end
    end

    Note over U,AC: The link has no /#/, but the web uses hash routes (/#/reset-password)
    U->>W: opens link, enters new password (12 to 64 characters, checked in the browser)
    W->>RL: POST /api/auth/reset-password {token, newPassword}
    alt rate limit exceeded
        RL-->>W: 429
    else within limit
        RL->>AC: ResetPassword(request)
        alt email, token or newPassword missing
            AC-->>W: 400 "Validation failed."
            Note over W,AC: The web sends no email, but the API requires it, so today the call stops here
        else signature bad or token expired
            AC-->>W: 400 "Invalid or expired reset token."
        else purpose or email claim does not match
            AC-->>W: 400 "Invalid token claims."
            Note over W,AC: A genuine token also lands here: it is read back as the short "email" claim,<br/>not ClaimTypes.Email (docs/ISSUES.md ISS-01)
        else token accepted
            AC->>AS: ResetPasswordAsync(request)
            AS->>DB: SELECT user, UPDATE PasswordHash (BCrypt)
            AS->>RT: RevokeAllUserTokensAsync(userId)
            AC-->>W: 200 "Password reset successfully."
            W-->>U: /login with "password reset" notice
        end
    end
